    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Unalakleet has long been a major trade hub linking Athabascan interior peoples with coastal Inupiat traders.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unalakleet%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1830s, Russian explorers established a trading post in Unalakleet under the Russian-American Company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unalakleet%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1898, the U.S. brought Sami reindeer herders from Lapland to Unalakleet to learn herding techniques.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unalakleet%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 1901 U.S. Army Signal Corps built a 605‑mile telegraph line that passed through Unalakleet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unalakleet%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Unalakleet experiences a subarctic climate with strong maritime influences, keeping winters milder than inland areas.",
